From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:20:30 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Home weather: lead forecast with the night's low, later
 periods beside it

Concept C from the November 6 weather-strip review. The first NWS period leads
(icon, high / low, a one-sentence summary); a daytime lead pairs with the night
after it. The next two periods follow as ruled rows with right-aligned temps.
Stacked in the 1024-1919px masthead ear, a row on tablets and from 1920px.
Icons in the strip share one ink; the heading is visible at every width.

ForecastGlance (Shared/Data) builds the lead and summary; unit tests cover a
day lead and a night lead. The weather CSS spread over nine breakpoint blocks
is one base set plus the ear, tablet and 1920 overrides; the 599/600px one-offs
and two width-dependent hiding rules are retired from check-css.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BeSUhTLXvQhUDsTovwqjsi
